{"name":"Blank Space","hex":"#505150","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blank","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White or pale; without colour.","Free from writing, printing, or marks; having an empty space to be filled in."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small French coin, originally of silver, afterwards of copper, worth 5 deniers; also a silver coin of Henry V current in the parts of France then held by the English, worth about 8 pence. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A nonplus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blank"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"}],"entries":[{"title":"Space (punctuation)","blocks":[{"text":"In writing, a space is a blank area that separates words, sentences, and other written or printed glyphs (characters). Conventions for spacing vary among languages, and in some languages the spacing rules are complex. Inter-word spaces ease the reader's task of identifying words, and avoid outright ambiguities such as \"now here\" vs. \"nowhere\". They also provide convenient guides for where a human or program may start new lines."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_(punctuation)"},{"title":"Whitespace character","blocks":[{"text":"A whitespace character is a character data element that represents white space when text is\nrendered for display by a computer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitespace_character"},{"title":"Blank Space","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blank Space\" is a song by the American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift and the second single from her fifth studio album, 1989 (2014). She wrote the song with its producers, Max Martin and Shellback. Inspired by the media scrutiny on Swift's love life that affected her girl-next-door reputation, \"Blank Space\" portrays a flirtatious woman with multiple romantic attachments. It is an electropop track with a minimal arrangement consisting of synthesizers, hip-hop-influenced beats, and layered vocals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/Taylor_Swift_-_Blank_Space_%28Official_Single_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blank_Space"},{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over whether it is itself an entity, a relationship between entities, or part of a conceptual framework."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/3D_coordinate_system.svg/330px-3D_coordinate_system.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Traditional_spacing_examples_from_the_1911_Chicago_Manual_of_Style.png/500px-Traditional_spacing_examples_from_the_1911_Chicago_Manual_of_Style.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Traditional_spacing_examples_from_the_1911_Chicago_Manual_of_Style.png/500px-Traditional_spacing_examples_from_the_1911_Chicago_Manual_of_Style.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Chicago Manual of Style has rules for using the different sized whitespaces.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraditional_spacing_examples_from_the_1911_Chicago_Manual_of_Style.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg/500px-OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg/1280px-OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg/500px-OHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The video was primarily shot at Oheka Castle in Long Island, New York.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOHEKA_CASTLE_exterior_view_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg/1280px-Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_010_%2818117338380%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swift performing \"Blank Space\" during the 1989 World Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaylor_Swift_010_(18117338380).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Gottfried_Wilhelm_Leibniz%2C_Bernhard_Christoph_Francke.jpg/500px-Gottfried_Wilhelm_Lei